  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Resilient and Nutrition Sensitive Agricultural Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The overall objective of the action is to promote food and nutrition security and food systems resilience in Nyaruguru, Gatsibo and Gakenke districts. This &lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34);&quot;&gt;will be achieved through two specific objectives/outcomes;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Outcome 1&lt;/strong&gt;: Increased food production and incomes through inclusive and sustainable management of agroecosystems,&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Outcome 2&lt;/strong&gt;: Enhanced nutrition and dietary intake&amp;nbsp;among malnourished children under 5 years and pregnant and lactating women.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The following outputs will contribute to the achievement of the above objectives;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Output 1.1&lt;/strong&gt;: Strengthened capacity of smallholder farmers to adopt climate-resilient agricultural practices,&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Output 1.2&lt;/strong&gt;: Increased availability and access to quality agricultural inputs,&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Output 1.3&lt;/strong&gt;: The capacities of farmers on post-harvest handling practices, smallholder aggregation&amp;nbsp;and livelihood diversification are enhanced,&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Output 2.1&lt;/strong&gt;: Appropriate maternal, infant, and young child nutrition (MIYCN) and water, sanitation, and hygiene (WASH) practices at household level are promoted,&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Output 2.2&lt;/strong&gt;: Strengthen district nutrition and WASH coordination mechanisms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
